\ ==== recurse ====

\ recurse ( -- ): compile a call to the innermost definition being compiled --
\ the enclosing quotation if inside one, else the enclosing colon word. Lets an
\ anonymous quotation self-call. An ordinary recursive call (pushes a return
\ frame per level); compile error outside a definition.

\ === anonymous quotation self-calls: factorial ===
[: dup 1 > if dup 1 - recurse * then :] to fact-q
5 fact-q execute . cr                   \ 120
0 fact-q execute . cr                   \ 0
1 fact-q execute . cr                   \ 1

\ === recurse in a colon word body ===
: fact  dup 1 > if dup 1 - recurse * then ;
6 fact . cr                             \ 720

\ === a quotation nested in a colon word: recurse targets the quotation ===
: sumdown  [: dup 0 = if else dup 1 - recurse + then :] execute ;
3 sumdown . cr                          \ 6
10 sumdown . cr                         \ 55

\ === errors (reason parenthesized) ===
recurse                                 \ (outside any definition)

clear

\ ==== tailcall ====

\ Tail-call elimination: a call whose only continuation is the terminal exit
\ (directly, or through unconditional branches and the trailing leave-locals) is
\ compiled to (tailcall), which reuses the current return frame -- so tail
\ recursion runs in constant return-stack space. Disabled when the body uses the
\ return stack or a prompt (>r r> r@ reset shift fail), or has locals and builds a
\ quotation (which could capture a local the tail-callee outlives). amb needs no
\ exclusion -- it removes its own choice mark before returning.

\ === deep self tail recursion runs in constant space (overflows without TCE) ===
: countdown  dup 0 = if drop else 1 - recurse then ;
1000000 countdown  42 . cr             \ 42

\ === tail recursion with an accumulator local, deep ===
: sum-to  | n acc | n 0 = if acc else n 1 - n acc + recurse then ;
1000000 0 sum-to . cr                  \ 500000500000

\ === both arms of if/else in tail position become (tailcall) ===
: leg1  1 + ;
: leg2  2 + ;
: split  dup 0 = if drop leg1 else drop leg2 then ;
' split see-compiled

\ === a return-stack word (>r) disables TCE: the self-call stays plain ===
: guarded  dup 0 = if drop else 5 >r r> drop 1 - recurse then ;
' guarded see-compiled

\ === locals + a quotation disables TCE: the map call stays plain and correct ===
: bump to k  k [ 10 20 30 ] [: 2 pick + :] map nip ;
100 bump . cr                          \ [ 110 120 130 ]

clear

\ ==== defer ====

\ defer ( "name" -- ), embodies ( xt "name" -- ), embodies! ( xt "name" -- ):
\ defer declares a forward-referenced word with no target; embodies installs a
\ target xt (a colon word or quotation), retargetable through one forwarding
\ dispatch; embodies! finalizes -- it rewrites every existing call site to call
\ the target directly and turns the deferred word into an ordinary word. Targets
\ are colon words or quotations; both embodies words are top-level only.

\ === mutual recursion across a forward reference ===
defer even?
: odd?  dup 0 = if drop false else 1 - even? then ;
[: dup 0 = if drop true else 1 - odd? then :] embodies even?
10 even? . cr                           \ 1
7 even? . cr                            \ 0
7 odd? . cr                             \ 1
0 odd? . cr                             \ 0

\ === embodies retargets: the newest target wins ===
defer greet
[: "hi" :] embodies greet
greet . cr                              \ hi
[: "bye" :] embodies greet
greet . cr                              \ bye

\ === embodies! finalizes; the recursion keeps working, now with direct calls ===
defer pick
: use-pick  pick 1 + ;
[: 41 :] embodies! pick
use-pick . cr                           \ 42

\ === a xt captured before embodies! still resolves, through the forwarder ===
defer late
' late
[: 7 :] embodies! late
execute . cr                            \ 7

\ === errors (reason parenthesized) ===
clear
defer unset
defer plus-five
5 ' + curry embodies plus-five
7 plus-five . cr                        \ 12  a curried token materializes into the deferred target

5 unset                                 \ (call before a target is installed)
[: 1 :] embodies nope-xyz               \ (embodies on an unknown word)
: plain 1 ;
[: 1 :] embodies plain                  \ (embodies on a non-deferred word)
defer d1
5 embodies d1                           \ (target is not an execution token)
' + embodies d1                         \ (target is a primitive, not a colon word/quotation)
defer d2
: bad-embodies  [: 1 :] embodies d2 ;   \ (embodies inside a definition)
defer d3
[: 1 :] embodies! d3
[: 2 :] embodies d3                     \ (re-embodying a now-ordinary word)

clear
